<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tzachas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1093</span> · Also known as Chaka Bey, Çaka Bey</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tzachas, called Chaka by the Turks, was a Seljuk Turkish emir who ruled Smyrna on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> from about 1088. A former captive at the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikephoros-iii-botaneiates">Nikephoros III</a>, he built a fleet, seized Aegean islands such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lesbos">Lesbos</a> and Chios and allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pechenegs">Pechenegs</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a>. Alexios I persuaded his son-in-law, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilij-arslan-i">Kilij Arslan I</a>, to kill him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tzachas.jpg" alt="Tzachas" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: VikiPicture · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C3%87aka_Bey_(Tzachas)_bust_at_Istanbul_Naval_Museum.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
